            <ArticleTitle>Low back pain as the presenting symptom of metastatic angiosarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>180-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is presented of a patient with the chief complaint of low back pain, who subsequently was found to have lumbar metastatic angiosarcoma. This report emphasizes the need for a thorough medical evaluation in all instances of radicular low back pain. The characteristics of metastatic intramedullary spinal cord tumor are outlined.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
